          "message": "[Perf][Qwen3] Enable QK norm RoPE cache fusion for dense models (#1766)\n\n* perf(qwen3): enable QK norm RoPE cache fusion for dense models\n\nDense Qwen3 currently applies Q/K RMSNorm before entering Attention, so\nQK norm, RoPE, per-token KV quantization, and cache writes run as separate\noperations. Qwen3-MoE already wires the same attention structure through\nAITER's fused_qk_norm_rope_cache_quant_shuffle kernel.\n\nReuse that existing path for dense Qwen3 when\nATOM_ENABLE_QK_NORM_ROPE_CACHE_QUANT_FUSION=1. Build the joint RoPE cache,\npass Q/K norm modules and packed QKV into Attention, and preserve the\ncurrent unfused fallback when the flag is disabled.\n\nThe flag remains disabled by default, matching the existing upstream\nbehavior. Update its documentation to cover both dense and MoE Qwen3 and\nadd source-level regression tests for the wiring and fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(qwen3): remove standalone fusion wiring test\n\nRemove the source-level fusion wiring test per reviewer feedback. Existing\nQwen3 and environment tests continue to cover the surrounding model and flag\ninfrastructure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* style(qwen3): align imports with Ruff and Black\n\nApply the import grouping requested by the Pre Checkin Ruff job and remove the\nextra blank line flagged by Black.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
